title: no "internal imports"
pid: c7c4f985-39b4-4aa3-9182-09b40ed07497
body: |2-
    In Rust it is valid to use 'use' statements in a function,
    or to qualify a long name in a type signature
    using the double-colon notation: _::_::_::_...
    I find that hard to read, and prefer to limit such notation
    to the initial, 'use' preamble of each file.
